Pass USE_CAUSAL and USE_PER_SEQ_CAUSAL to the INT4 tile-loop bounds.

compute_tile_loop_bounds declares both as constexpr with defaults (True, False),
and v1/attention/ops/int4_per_token_head.py's call stops at IS_3D. The generic
kernel passes them (triton_unified_attention.py). So the INT4 tile loop always
takes the causal branch and ends at

    context_len + q_block_local_idx * BLOCK_Q + (BLOCK_M - 1) // G + 1

The per-element mask in compute_kv_seq_mask does get both -- but it can only
mask keys the loop already read, so the newest KV positions are simply absent.

Reachable through the DFlash2 drafter, which is non-causal (config.json:
is_causal false, 5 sliding_attention layers, 32 query heads / 8 KV heads,
head_dim 128) and takes the target's kv_cache_dtype. At BLOCK_M 16 and G 4 the
bound is 4, so every verify block longer than 4 loses KV; at DFLASH_TOKENS=7 the
block is 8 and it fires on every step.

Measured on an RTX 4080 SUPER, drafter geometry, 2048 tokens, against the same
kernel with the two arguments added, warm clock:

  query len   causal          non-causal
  1 .. 4      bit-identical   bit-identical
  5, 6, 8, 12 bit-identical   rel 4.167e-03
  16          bit-identical   rel 1.250e-02

Same result with sliding_window (2047, 0) as in production. The causal path is
bit-identical at every length tested, so this changes only the non-causal one.

--- a/v1/attention/ops/int4_per_token_head.py
+++ b/v1/attention/ops/int4_per_token_head.py
@@ -512,6 +512,8 @@
         SLIDING_WINDOW,
         USE_MM_PREFIX,
         IS_3D,
+        USE_CAUSAL,
+        USE_PER_SEQ_CAUSAL,
     )
 
     # Tile loop.  Per-tile: load packed KV + scales, dequantize into
